  "name": null,
  "problem": "The eagle's path traces a curve $C$ in the $xy$-plane. Suppose that the eagle is at the point $P$ on $C$ at time $t.$ Expressed in terms of $t,$ what function gives the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The slope of the tangent to $C$ at time $t$ equals$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "The slope of the tangent to $C$ equals $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$ To calculate this, we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nIn parts 1 and 2, we found\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}},\\,{y}^{′}(t)={t}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{t}^{2}-2}{(\\frac{5}{25+{t}^{2}})}=\\frac{1}{5}({t}^{2}-2)({t}^{2}+25).\n$$",
